@startuml
title Bitcoin Self-Custody WhatsApp Consultancy — System Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"

actor "Client A\n(WhatsApp user)" as ClientA #LightBlue
actor "Client B\n(WhatsApp user)" as ClientB #LightGreen
actor "You\n(Admin)" as Admin #Gold

cloud "WhatsApp\nServers\n(E2E encrypted)" as WA #White

package "Host Machine\n(Windows 10 OR Linux VPS)" as Host #F8F8F8 {

    package "Hermes Profile: 'btc-consult'\n(~/.hermes/profiles/btc-consult/)" as Profile #EAEAFF {

        component "Baileys Bridge\nNode.js, unofficial\nWhatsApp Web emulation" as Baileys #LightYellow
        component "Gateway\n(session router,\ncron scheduler)" as Gateway #LightYellow

        component "AIAgent\n(conversation loop,\ntool dispatch,\nprompt builder)" as Agent #FFE4B5

        database "state.db\nSQLite + FTS5" as DB {
            rectangle "Session A\n(key=chatA+userA)" as SA
            rectangle "Session B\n(key=chatB+userB)" as SB
            rectangle "Admin session" as SAdm
        }

        file "SOUL.md\nBitcoin consultant\npersona" as Soul #FFFACD
        file "config.yaml\ntoolsets, approvals,\ncompression, etc." as Config #FFFACD
        file ".env\nAPI keys" as Env #FFFACD
        file "MEMORY.md\n(profile-wide)" as Mem #FFB6C1
        file "gateway.json\nreset policies,\nplatform config" as GW #FFFACD

        rectangle "Tool Layer" as Tools {
            component "Web Search" as WebT
            component "Web Extract" as ExtT
            component "Vision Analyze" as VisionT
            component "STT: faster-whisper" as STT
            component "TTS: edge" as TTS
        }
    }
}

cloud "LLM Provider\n(OpenRouter / Anthropic /\nNous Portal / Gemini)" as LLM #E0E0FF
cloud "Internet\n(BTC price, news,\nwallet docs)" as Internet #E0FFE0

ClientA --> WA : text / voice / image
ClientB --> WA : text / voice / image
WA --> Baileys : encrypted payload
Baileys --> Gateway : normalized message\n(chat_id, user_id, body)
Gateway --> DB : lookup session by\nhash(chat_id, user_id)

Gateway --> Agent : turn (User A)\nloads ONLY Session A history
Gateway --> Agent : turn (User B)\nloads ONLY Session B history

Agent --> Soul : read persona\n(system prompt slot one)
Agent --> Config : read enabled toolsets
Agent --> Mem : retrieve relevant facts\n(RISK: profile-wide!)
Agent --> LLM : chat completion\n(with tools schema)
Agent --> WebT : BTC price / news lookup
Agent --> VisionT : wallet screenshot analysis
Agent --> STT : transcribe inbound .ogg voice
Agent --> TTS : synthesize outbound MP3 voice

WebT --> Internet
ExtT --> Internet
VisionT --> LLM : uses LLM vision model

Agent --> Gateway : final text + tool results
Gateway --> Baileys : outbound msg\n(markdown → WhatsApp fmt)
Baileys --> WA : encrypted
WA --> ClientA : reply
WA --> ClientB : reply

Admin --> Profile : `hermes -p btc-consult`\n(config, /approve, /restart,\nmonitor logs, prune sessions)

note bottom of DB #E0FFE0
  <b>ISOLATION GUARANTEE (the core ask)</b>
  Session key = deterministic hash(chat_id, user_id)
  Client A's message history NEVER enters Client B's context.
  Cross-session reads are blocked at the session store layer.
  This is true even though all sessions live in one SQLite file.
end note

note right of Mem #FFE4E1
  <b>MEMORY LEAKAGE RISK (must address)</b>
  Default MEMORY.md is shared across ALL sessions in the profile.
  If Client A says "I use a Ledger Nano X", that fact could
  surface when Client B asks about hardware wallets.

  Mitigations (pick one):
   1. Disable memory entirely — `memory.memory_enabled: false`
   2. Use Honcho backend — per-user memory partitioning
      (`hermes honcho setup`, requires honcho plugin)
   3. Keep memory but instruct agent to NEVER store client data,
      only generic Bitcoin expertise (fragile — not recommended)

  Recommended: Option 1 (disable) for v1 launch, Honcho for v2.
end note

note bottom of Tools #E0E0FF
  <b>TOOLSET LOCKDOWN</b>
  ENABLED:  web, vision, stt, tts  (consultancy value)
  DISABLED: terminal, file, code_execution, cronjob,
            delegation, session_search, skills, kanban,
            clarify (clients can't ask clarifying Qs to admin)

  Rationale: clients must not run shell, read host files,
  or schedule jobs on your machine.
  Consider the bundled `safe` toolset as a starting base.
end note

note right of Baileys #FFFACD
  <b>BAN RISK</b>
  Baileys is unofficial. Mitigate:
   - Dedicated phone number (NOT personal)
   - No bulk/outbound spam
   - Only reply to inbound messages
   - Keep session keys safe (~/.hermes/platforms/whatsapp/session)
end note

@enduml